INT. PARKING GARAGE ELEVATOR - NIGHT

Stopped. Between floors. One flickering tube. Brushed steel, scratched.

BRYNJA LARSEN, forties, a lawyer's briefcase. Pressed against the wall.

RUFUS BELLAMY, fifties, a janitor's jumpsuit. Mop bucket at his feet.

CALLISTA MOREAU, twenties, earbuds. Texting. No signal.

BRYNJA
Press the button again.

RUFUS
I pressed it.

BRYNJA
Again.

He does. Nothing. The light flickers.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
(distorted)
Hello? Is someone in the car?

BRYNJA
Yes! Three of us!

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Please remain calm. Maintenance is en route.

CALLISTA
How long?

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Forty minutes.

RUFUS
(muttering)
Forty minutes.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Is anyone carrying a bag?

Brynja's grip tightens on the briefcase. Rufus glances at it. Callista looks up from her phone.

CALLISTA
Why?

The intercom crackles. Then, very quietly:

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Because the sensor says the car is heavier than it should be.
